WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Beyond the heavy rain is a rainbow
hageshii ame no mukou kakaru niji wo mita

3
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.170
I'll know the easy answer's a lie
tayasui kotae wa uso dato shiru darou

4
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Vow not to back down to the shouting
dekai koe nanka ni makenai to chikatte

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
I need you alone to understand tomorrow
anata hitori ni wakatte hoshii ashita

6
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.770
You gave me the time of my life
yume no youna jikan kureta anata

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:51.280
What do I look like? An ANGEL or a DEVIL...
watashi wa dou mieteruno? sorega tenshi ka akuma ka

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.240
Beyond the dawn, beyond the dawn
yoake no mukou yoake no mukou

9
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.740
There's so much I want to tell you
hanashitai koto takusan arun da

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.540
Filled with love, with love
ai kometa ai kometa

11
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.460
That can't be written down in a letter
tegami ni kakikirenai omoi da

12
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:20.890
A small hand in search of eternity
eien wo sagashita chiisana tenohira

13
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:39.280
<b>"To Save His Daughter -
Kuma the Timid Pacifist"</b>

14
00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.000
Carry the seriously injured to the church!

15
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:53.710
Can somebody give us a hand?!

16
00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:55.670
He's back!

17
00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:16.240
It's awful... Our houses...

18
00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.360
Why... Why did they do this?!

19
00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.570
I won't forgive you, Bekori!

20
00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.830
Wait, Kuma! That's enough!

21
00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.830
You can't save anyone now!

22
00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:33.340
Mommy!

23
00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:36.710
No! No!

24
00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:38.880
Hey, Kuma!

25
00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.680
Come back! You're gonna die!

26
00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.650
In a country far to the east,
this same approach was so successful...

27
00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.230
...that the Celestial Dragons
praised their town...

28
00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.150
...for being beautiful
and free of "garbage."

29
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.870
That's great!

30
00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:07.450
For the sake of the people, the country,
and the immense happiness of the population,

31
00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:11.830
we must sometimes be ruthless
and carry out reforms...

32
00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.170
King Bekori!

33
00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:18.170
Furious protesters have gathered
at the gate of the castle!

34
00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.050
Murderers!

35
00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.550
Stop it now!

36
00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:26.760
Put out the fires in the south!

37
00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.190
- Don't go any further!
- Back off!

38
00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.160
Shoot four or five.
It's for the greater good.

39
00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.530
No!

40
00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:48.490
How could you do this?!

41
00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.710
Those who dare defy the king's edict,
step forward!

42
00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:06.100
Hm? Who's that?

43
00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.890
Execute him right here!

44
00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.150
<b>Kuma's Church</b>

45
00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.280
Hurry and treat the wounded!

46
00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.570
Bonney-chan, stay inside. You don't want 
to be exposed to the moonlight.

47
00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:26.570
Okay.

48
00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:31.160
I hope he's safe... 
Dad's always such a chicken.

49
00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.750
W-Wait!

50
00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.620
What do you want?!

51
00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.500
Oh, I know! I'll grant you
all the area that I burned down!

52
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:42.010
I got rid of the human garbage!

53
00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.400
Mommy!

54
00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.470
Wait, you bastard!

55
00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:29.930
You know what'll happen
if you attack the king!

56
00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.930
You'll pay dearly for this!

57
00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.810
The World Government won't
tolerate this atrocity!

58
00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:41.770
You country-bumpkin pastor!

59
00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:53.700
This incident would be known as the 
Solo Revolution of the Sorbet Kingdom.

60
00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.210
<b>Holy Land 
Mary Geoise</b>

61
00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:00.040
It appears the king of
the Sorbet Kingdom has been replaced.

62
00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.130
That's strange. By whom?

63
00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:06.420
Kuma! Kuma!

64
00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:07.840
- King Kuma!
- Kuma!

65
00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.050
Kuma! Kuma!

66
00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.310
Unable to refuse the people's wishes,

67
00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:19.350
Kuma became the king who kept 
living in his old church.

68
00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.060
King Kumachi!

69
00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.730
My back hurts!

70
00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.690
I think you can stop teasing me now.

71
00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.410
It's Mr. Bulldog who is actually
running the country from the palace.

72
00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.370
I'm just a figurehead
to make everyone feel secure.

73
00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:39.580
Back in King Bulldog's day,
two generations ago, we were poor,

74
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:41.540
but we were spiritually rich.

75
00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:44.170
Being poor was the pits though.

76
00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.340
Oh? Where is Bonney-chan?

77
00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.390
Oh, she is exercising there...

78
00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.260
Oh? Where did she go?

79
00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:59.100
Stamina! Stamina!

80
00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:00.850
Have I ever seen that girl?

81
00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:03.440
She looks just as pretty as Ginny!

82
00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:06.530
What?! Ginny?!

83
00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:11.780
Why are you all so shocked?

84
00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:17.240
On my tenth birthday,
I'll sail out to the sea with Dad

85
00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.790
and see the horizon!

86
00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.870
What?! "Dad"?

87
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:23.330
So I'm building up stamina...

88
00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.500
What?!

89
00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.510
What?! You're Bonney?!

90
00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:39.390
What was that transformation?!

91
00:07:39.430 --> 00:07:41.560
Was it a Devil Fruit power?
When did you eat it?

92
00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.110
Kumachi! Stay with me!

93
00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.910
Maybe this is it... The Age-Age Fruit.

94
00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:55.570
But where did she get it?

95
00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:58.240
Try to make it happen.

96
00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:06.630
Get older! Get older!

97
00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:09.710
Wait, Bonney! I can't take it anymore!

98
00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.430
King Kuma! Grant me an audience with you!

99
00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.850
She really turned into an old bag!

100
00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.100
Damn! She's full of wrinkles!

101
00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:25.350
Look, Kumachi!

102
00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.900
It's not working. I can't get older.

103
00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.900
You're Princess Bonney, aren't you?

104
00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.190
Who are you, old man?

105
00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:36.450
I'm Bulldog. I'm an aide to your father.

106
00:08:36.450 --> 00:08:39.370
<b>Bulldog, Former King 
(Two Generations Ago) 
of the Sorbet Kingdom</b>

107
00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.370
I have something important to tell your father.

108
00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:42.450
My mother is already here.

109
00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.250
Conney, the former queen dowager.

110
00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.960
<b>Conney, Former Queen Dowager</b>

111
00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:48.540
- Our sincerest apologies!
- Sorry!

112
00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.170
That's okay.

113
00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.390
Look at this terrible rubbish!

114
00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.140
"Evil Dictator"

115
00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:02.560
It says Kuma burned down a village
and took the throne with violence!

116
00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:04.890
Evidently, Bekori is behind this.

117
00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:08.360
That bastard!
He's using a dirty trick while in exile!

118
00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.190
He has the World Government on his side.

119
00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:15.110
He'll come to take back the throne for sure.

120
00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:19.030
There are reports of
warships being prepared.

121
00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.490
No!

122
00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:23.410
I don't want him back!

123
00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.160
He'll have us killed this time!

124
00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.040
We were finally able to live
with peace of mind.

125
00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:34.210
I know. If he comes back,

126
00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:37.180
I'll fight back
and destroy every force he musters!

127
00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:43.770
But then I'll be branded as a criminal.
I won't be able to stay in this country.

128
00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:48.650
When that happens, Bulldog-san,
I want you to take the throne!

129
00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.400
I got bigger!

130
00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.700
And I need you to shelter Bonney.

131
00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.070
This church will be in danger.

132
00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.320
- I did it!
- No problem.

133
00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:02.990
I'll recreate this environment for her.

134
00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.120
Thank you.

135
00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:11.590
Bonney, I'll come back when I get a chance,
so be good.

136
00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:13.750
That's my mother.

137
00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.630
Bonney,
listen to Bulldog-san and Conney-san

138
00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.220
and be good.

139
00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.930
Are you going somewhere?
That makes me sad...

140
00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:26.140
To protect you and everyone in this country,
I must go.

141
00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.920
You've got some nerve coming back here!

142
00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:17.690
That's him, Marines!

143
00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:19.740
Kill him!

144
00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.990
He took the Sorbet Kingdom away from me!

145
00:11:24.070 --> 00:11:26.990
He's a tyrant who engages
in every kind of misrule!

146
00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.200
Kill him!

147
00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:31.920
I'm the king of this country!

148
00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:59.610
Naturally, after sinking all the ships
and fleeing to the sea,

149
00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:01.610
Kuma was placed on the wanted list as a pirate.

150
00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.740
His numerous notorious deeds and his strength...

151
00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.240
...drove up his bounty.

152
00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:10.620
Bonney-chan.

153
00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.790
The pizza is done.

154
00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.750
I miss Dad...

155
00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:18.420
I'm sorry, Bonney-chan.

156
00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:22.130
Kuma-san saved this country, he's a hero.

157
00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.050
I don't care! He's my daddy!

158
00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.020
When I turn ten and get well,
I'll become a pirate, too!

159
00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.690
You better not...

160
00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:39.020
I can even become an adult right now!

161
00:12:45.780 --> 00:12:49.280
From then on, Kuma traveled 
all over the world...

162
00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:52.120
...in search of a cure for Bonney.

163
00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:55.830
Do you know this disease?

164
00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.790
She can't be exposed to natural light.

165
00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:01.670
What?! She can't be in the sun?!

166
00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.720
How tragic...

167
00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.430
There he is! A guy with a high bounty!

168
00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.100
You're Bartholomew Kuma, aren't you?!

169
00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.450
Your daughter...

170
00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:32.160
...has five years at most to live.

171
00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:36.540
She won't live to see her tenth birthday.

172
00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.070
Come on!

173
00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.030
Hey!

174
00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:17.540
Kuma-chan! What are you doing here?!

175
00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:30.720
Iva and Inazuma were imprisoned.

176
00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:36.430
In our time apart, you've become
a king, a tyrant, and a pirate.

177
00:14:36.850 --> 00:14:38.230
It's like I'm a totally different person.

178
00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:42.810
No one in the Revolutionary Army
would fall for that article.

179
00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:45.940
Hey, Kuma!

180
00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:49.450
I wanna become the captain of the 
Eastern Forces. What do you say?

181
00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:52.200
Why are you asking me, Betty?

182
00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:55.870
Dragon-san said until Kuma permits it,

183
00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.370
it'd be held vacant in Ginny-sama's honor.

184
00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:02.080
The Eastern Forces will be
led by a sharp-tongued woman?

185
00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.340
I don't mind.

186
00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:06.210
Ya-hoo! Hup!

187
00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:10.840
Guys, here comes
the new captain of the Eastern Forces!

188
00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:13.680
Sabo, Koala, and the others
are wishing to see you, too.

189
00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:16.850
The young revolutionaries
are steadily gaining power.

190
00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.850
I wish I could show it to you.

191
00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.640
I'm happy for you!

192
00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:22.310
I know you are.

193
00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.730
It's great to have comrades...

194
00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:31.660
I've seen what's happening in the world and
 often wondered what you would have done.

195
00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.990
I want to return to your army, but...

196
00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:40.660
I wanted to talk to you about Bonney.

197
00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:46.000
You know Dr. Vegapunk,
the Marines' scientist, right?

198
00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:46.920
Yeah.

199
00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.970
Seems like after the accident the other day,
he's going to move to a new lab.

200
00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:55.260
He's normally not someone
you can easily meet,

201
00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.810
but right now,
the security is evidently lax.

202
00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:02.560
You think he can cure Bonney?!

203
00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.100
Maybe...

204
00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:13.660
He's an odd man,
but he's driven by his desires and trustworthy.

205
00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.070
You should meet him.

206
00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.950
- Take care, Kuma-chan!
- Bye, Kuma!

207
00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:22.040
Thank you, Dragon!
To be honest, I had almost given up.

208
00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.670
I'll go see him!

209
00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:28.420
If Bonney gets better,

210
00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.380
I want to fight with you again!

211
00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:36.300
Let the winds of fate carry us
where they will, my friend.

212
00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:38.300
Mm-hm!

213
00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:42.890
- Bon voyage!
- Take care!

214
00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:49.400
Let the winds of fate carry us
where they will...

215
00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:55.860
Bonney! I'm back!

216
00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:00.660
Dad!

217
00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.580
You're so strong!

218
00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:06.040
Well, I went easy on her...

219
00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:09.000
How have you been?

220
00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:13.880
Great! I'm building up stamina every day
so I can go out to sea at any time!

221
00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:17.010
Good! Then let's go out to sea!

222
00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:18.720
Really?!

223
00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.100
Where are we?

224
00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:28.060
<b>Marines' Science Group,
 Laboratory 8 
(Later Known as Egghead)</b>

225
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:27.730
We're seeing a doctor to get a checkup 
before your disease is healed.

226
00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.230
W-What?!

227
00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:33.400
I-I've never seen anyone like you before!

228
00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:36.360
I was thinking the same...

229
00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:38.530
What a magnificent build!

230
00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:42.790
Let me study your muscles!
In the name of science!

231
00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:47.170
Hey, Dad! Let me see!

232
00:17:50.960 --> 00:17:53.590
Look at that head. Gross...

233
00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.470
Is she the sick girl?

234
00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:56.880
What a sassy brat.

235
00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.300
I don't hate it though.

236
00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.430
Oh, Sapphire Scales, huh?

237
00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.940
You've done well
to keep it from spreading more.

238
00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:08.810
What do you think?

239
00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:09.770
It's curable!

240
00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:10.980
Are you sure?!

241
00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:12.980
Yeah...

242
00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.490
Yay! Yay! Yay!

243
00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:26.620
I'll be using technology
not yet introduced in clinical medicine!

244
00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:31.540
Specifically, I'll create stem cells
and transplant them.

245
00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:35.340
But to do so, it'll require a lot of time
and money, like creating a cyborg.

246
00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:37.220
Is she gonna become a cyborg?!

247
00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.800
It'll cost as much, I said!

248
00:18:43.470 --> 00:18:46.100
Are you a Buccaneer?!

249
00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:46.850
Yeah.

250
00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.770
Hey, I'm on the Government's side!

251
00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.480
I trust Dragon.

252
00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:55.020
What makes my blood different from others?

253
00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:05.200
I don't have enough samples
to explain that in detail, but...

254
00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:09.120
My clones?!

255
00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:10.420
That's right!

256
00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:14.210
I've been looking for the right person
to be the base for my clone soldiers!

257
00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:17.840
If you donate your blood and give me
 permission to create clone soldiers,

258
00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:22.050
you won't have to pay for
the immense cost of Bonney's procedure.

259
00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:23.510
You don't have money, right?

260
00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:26.680
I won't decline that offer either way,

261
00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:28.470
but can I ask what they'll do?

262
00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:31.900
There'll be soldiers who look like me,

263
00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:33.810
and they'll work for the Marines?

264
00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.480
That's the idea!

265
00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.230
Do you like electromagnetic energy?

266
00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:41.530
If a human being shoots laser beams,

267
00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.870
it'll shock pirates speechless!

268
00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:47.910
We'll use our overwhelming scientific power
to defeat the rascals!

269
00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:53.170
The sturdy bodies of my soldiers will act
as shields to repel bullets and save the weak!

270
00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.920
They'll become heroes!

271
00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.960
And furthermore,
the mighty warriors from the future will...

272
00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.090
Dragon said what?!

273
00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:05.510
He said you were an odd man, but you were
driven by your desires and trustworthy.

274
00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:08.510
Is that what he said?
What a whipper-snapper!

275
00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:14.270
If a clone soldier in my likeness
saves someone's life one day,

276
00:20:14.310 --> 00:20:17.020
then maybe my being born
wasn't for nothing.

277
00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:20.650
Dragon will be furious about these terms.

278
00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.280
Well, I have nothing
but gratitude for you both.

279
00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:28.700
To be honest, if Bonney could survive,

280
00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:31.120
I wouldn't have cared if you were a devil.

281
00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:35.960
Please save Bonney!

282
00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:39.420
You're a true saint.

283
00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.300
Clone soldiers are weapons.

284
00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:49.970
And weapons are judged
by how many people they can kill.

285
00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:55.060
Vegapunk would let a golden opportunity 
slip through his fingers.

286
00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:57.810
But I have a plan.

287
00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:00.190
Yes, sir! I'm at your command!

288
00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:02.070
A saint?

289
00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:08.570
I'm just a timid pacifist who wants peace.

290
00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:11.910
I like that!

291
00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:14.540
I'll use that as the name for
the warriors of the future!

292
00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:37.020
I can't protect anyone again
mata daremo mamorenai no

293
00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.820
It's my fault that the voice is fading away
kiekakaru koe wa boku no sei

294
00:21:41.820 --> 00:21:44.110
I don't even have time to look down
utsumuku hima mo nai no

295
00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.700
Gravel marks on my palms
tenohira ni tsuku jari no ato

296
00:21:46.700 --> 00:21:50.080
Start moving again, my ship
mata ugokidase boku no fune yo

297
00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:55.580
Though I can't fly in the broad sky
hiroi sora wa tobenai kedo

298
00:21:55.580 --> 00:22:01.460
I can light up the deep sea
fukai umi wa teraseru kara

299
00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:02.420
We
bokura wa

300
00:22:02.510 --> 00:22:04.920
EVERYDAY owarenai
EVERYDAY, can't let this be the end

301
00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.550
EVERYDAY makerenai
EVERYDAY, can't be defeated

302
00:22:07.550 --> 00:22:11.310
We have something here to protect
mamoru mono ga koko niwa aru

303
00:22:11.350 --> 00:22:13.850
This may not be what I expected
yosou chigai kamo?

304
00:22:13.930 --> 00:22:16.560
But we can't stop now
tomarenai yo mou

305
00:22:16.640 --> 00:22:21.860
We go on, sharing loneliness
kodoku wo ima wakeai susumu

306
00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:24.610
Don't be afraid
ojikedzukuna yo

307
00:22:24.690 --> 00:22:28.570
I'm not the same person I was that day
ano hi no boku to chigau kara

308
00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:32.030
No one can stand in my way
dare nimo jama dekinai yo

309
00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:33.660
Now, move aside
saa doite

310
00:22:33.700 --> 00:22:36.250
Conquer the world, believe in the future
sekai wo seishite mirai wo shinjite

311
00:22:36.370 --> 00:22:38.830
Count up the nights
ikutsu mono yoru kazoete

312
00:22:38.830 --> 00:22:41.540
What did you see? What did you learn?
nani wo mite nani wo shitte

313
00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.550
To realize what was important
taisetsu na koto ni kidzuita no
